  "notes": [
    "CAN 2.0A node (docs/extension-study.md section 7.2, revision 3): TXD on pin 0, RXD on pin 1, 500 kbit/s at 50 MHz (P = 50, 100 cycles per bit, sample point 50%). NRZ, stuffing after 5 equal bits, CRC-15 by the unit (preset 2, MSB first), arbitration monitor.",
    "Transmit, when the TX queue has data: 3 words per frame, a header word (SOF, ID, RTR, IDE, r0, DLC in bits 31..13) and 8 data bytes MSB first; the frame starts 150 cycles after LTIM (just after intermission). No ACK: fault 70. Arbitration lost: fault 72 (the header word is consumed; the host requeues).",
    "Receive otherwise: the header word (SOF..DLC in its low 19 bits; the upper bits are stale), then the data bytes packed MSB first into at most 2 words (DLC > 4: the first word holds the first DLC-4 bytes, the second the last 4; valid bytes are the low 8n bits). CRC error: fault 71. It drives the ACK slot dominant.",
    "Both frame tails end in the middle of the 2nd intermission bit, so an SOF in the 3rd intermission bit is received. Not implemented: error and overload frames, error counters, resynchronization, retry after arbitration loss, remote frames, extended IDs.",
    "Needs the line unit (options.line_unit rec16, docs/extension.md); assemble with --variant configs/variants/diet8_rec16.json."
  ]
